# Every storage tier gets a committed directory but never committed contents.
#
# The directories themselves must exist in a fresh clone: platform:doctor fails
# the deployment when a tier is missing, and the first upload into a tier that
# does not exist would fail on a host where the web user cannot create
# directories under storage/app. The per-directory .gitignore in each tier then
# keeps its contents out of git.
*
!authenticated/
!private/
!public/
!restricted/
!.gitignore
